data: {"type":"agent_chunk","agent":"analyst","content":"- **Core mechanism:** Cas9 paired with a synthetic guide RNA cuts DNA at a chosen site [1]. Programmable molecules create double-strand breaks that allow insertion, deletion, modification, or replacement of DNA [3].\n\n- **Natural origin:** CRISPR is a bacterial and archaeal DNA sequence family built from bacteriophage DNA, used to detect and destroy similar phage DNA [2]. The gene-editing tool is a simplified version of this antiviral system [1].\n\n- **Hype versus evidence:** A Hacker News post framed a CRISPR breakthrough as opening treatment for a broad range of diseases [4]. The supporting HIV result was limited to cell culture [5], so it does not show clinical efficacy."}

